# Kotlin/JVM specific
*.class
*.log
*.ctxt
.mtj.tmp/
*.jar
# Exception: the Gradle wrapper jar MUST be committed -- it's what lets
# gradlew/gradlew.bat bootstrap Gradle with zero local install required.
# Without this exception, `git add -A` silently drops it and gradlew.bat
# fails with "Could not find or load main class
# org.gradle.wrapper.GradleWrapperMain" for anyone who clones the repo --
# exactly what happened here, traced back to this missing negation rule
# in the original forked .gitignore. Using **/ so it matches regardless
# of which subfolder the Android project lives in (this repo is a
# monorepo with the app under android-app/, not at the root).
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
*.war
*.nar
*.ear
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

